// A call that recovered fewer arguments than the callee's declaration requires
// is padded with zeros.  The call is still built, so nothing downstream can
// tell that an argument was invented.  The default lift reports it as a
// warning and still lowers; `-strict` turns the report into an error and stops
// before lowering.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=TU %s --input-file %t.c
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
//
// WARN: Diag Warning: {{.*}}lossy lift [arg-synthesized]: call to 'ext_func' (operation 'call_ext') in function 'strict_arg_synthesized': 0 argument(s) were recovered but the declaration requires 1; the missing ones are filled with zero
// WARN-NOT: Diag Error
// TU: ext_func(0U);
// ERR: Diag Error: {{.*}}lossy lift [arg-synthesized]: call to 'ext_func' (operation 'call_ext') in function 'strict_arg_synthesized': 0 argument(s) were recovered but the declaration requires 1; the missing ones are filled with zero
// ERR: Skipping code generation due to prior diagnostics errors
